bitter:
And last year's leaves are smoke in every lane;
But last year's bitter loving must remain
Heaped on my heart, and my old thoughts abide!

bite:
I said just to try them:
“I’ll bite off your heads and give them to my little children to eat.”
But they didn’t believe I was a bird;

bitten:
And changes the first form of it. I’ve marked
A shore of pebbles bitten to one shape
From all the various life of madrepores;

bitterly:
Who with exceeding grief lamented Thee;
Not so fallen Peter weeping bitterly;
Not so the thief was moved;

bites:
The candle Fairy comes;
And if you play with it, it bites
Your fingers and your thumbs.

bitted:
Coursing far, coursing near,
Curbed his amber-bitted steed,
Coursed amain to hear;
